<p>Russian strikes hit several Ukrainian cities and energy sites on May 5, killing at least 28 people hours before a unilateral ceasefire proposed by Kyiv was set to begin at midnight on May 6, Ukrainian officials said. The dead included at least 12 people in Zaporizhzhia, five in Kramatorsk, four in Dnipro and five at gas production facilities in the Poltava and Kharkiv regions, according to Ukrainian officials and company statements carried by the reports. Russia announced a May 8-9 ceasefire to coincide with Victory Day commemorations and a Moscow military parade; Ukraine responded by proposing an open-ended ceasefire from midnight on May 6 and urged Moscow to reciprocate. After Kyiv&#x27;s declared pause began, Ukraine accused Russia of violating it with an attack on an industrial site in the Zaporizhzhia region and with attacks involving 108 combat drones and three missiles; Russia-appointed authorities in Crimea said a Ukrainian drone attack killed five civilians in Dzhankoi, though reports said it likely occurred before Kyiv&#x27;s midnight deadline.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kT8fxnhXsHraOR0-BlslCzpk-I8Jqlp7r-KfT8qYbYq3Ow7JK5uhKG89kHWgFb3CNTVHczPfkH1pzCdxE__hXT8n0p-rYito5gtNUNSVsBfp' alt='A site of a Russian air strike in Zaporizhzhia, Ukraine, on May 5, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strike methods: Ukrainian officials said the May 5 attacks involved glide bombs, drones and missiles, with aerial bombs hitting central Kramatorsk and guided bombs striking Zaporizhzhia.</li><li>Rescue risks: Officials said follow-on drone or missile strikes complicated emergency work, including at energy facilities in Poltava, where two rescue workers were among those killed.</li><li>Ukrainian response: Ukraine also struck inside Russia; reports cited a long-range missile attack on a Russian plant and a drone attack in Chuvashia that Russian state media said killed two people.</li><li>Victory Day security: A Taiwanese public broadcaster reported that Putin warned Kyiv against disrupting Russia&#x27;s Victory Day events and threatened large-scale missile retaliation if Ukraine interfered with the celebrations.</li></ul><blockquote>Russia could cease fire at any moment, and this would stop the war and our responses - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy: The Ukrainian president accused Moscow of &quot;utter cynicism&quot; for launching attacks while presenting its Victory Day truce as a peace gesture. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/06/g-s1-120377/zelenskyy-slams-russia-as-strikes-kill-22-in-ukraine'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Andrii Sybiha: Ukraine&#x27;s foreign minister said Russia&#x27;s actions showed it was not preparing for peace and accused Moscow of intensifying terror instead of ending hostilities. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458349/russian-attacks-kill-27-in-ukraine-ahead-of-proposed-ceasefire'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>Sergei Aksyonov: The Russia-appointed head of Crimea said the Dzhankoi incident was a Ukrainian strike on civilians in the annexed peninsula. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458349/russian-attacks-kill-27-in-ukraine-ahead-of-proposed-ceasefire'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>Naftogaz: Naftogaz chief Serhiy Koretskyi said the company was responding to damage to gas production infrastructure after a Russian missile-and-drone barrage. (<a href='https://www.dailymaverick.co.za/article/2026-05-05-russian-attack-kills-five-at-ukraines-naftogaz-gas-production-facilities-officials-say/'>Daily Maverick</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/ukraine-russia-strikes-flamingo-drones-/33750580.html'>More Than 20 Killed In Russian Strikes Across Ukraine; Kyiv Hits Russian Plant With Long-Range Missiles</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russian-attack-kills-two-in-ukraines-zaporizhzhia-governor-says'>Russian attacks kill 25 in Ukraine, hours before deadline for ceasefire proposed by Kyiv